// EXPECT: [E003]
// Locks the FIX of a former P0 compiler CRASH (type_move(NULL), old char README):
// matching a linear ADT — a variant with a `mov *u8` payload — and `mov`-consuming
// the binding in a `case` used to SEGFAULT the compiler. A crash or abort would make
// this test fail — so it guards the no-crash fix.
//
// The rejection CODE moved from [E012] to [E003], which records real progress: match-arm
// payload bindings are now DECLARED with their variant field's type, so `mov ptr` is a
// well-typed consume rather than a "binding has no owned value type" error. What remains
// is the other half — consuming the payload does not DISCHARGE the scrutinee, so `b`
// reports as unconsumed.
//
// Do not "fix" that by consuming the scrutinee wholesale when a non-borrowed `case`
// destructures it. That rule was tried and is UNSOUND: it discharges the obligation
// without anyone releasing the resource, and accepts BOTH `Full(ptr): free(ptr);
// free(ptr)` (double free) and `Full(ptr): noop()` (leak). Discharging correctly needs the
// payload binding to be linear in its own right — per-field state, which the new IR pass
// has (src/analysis/linearity.h) and this one does not. This test flips to a _pass when
// that lands. Tracked in TRACEABILITY (§15).
import std.mem.{mem_free}
type Box {
    Full {
        ptr mov *u8
    }
    Empty
}
proc noop() {
    var x = 0
}
proc t(b mov Box) {
    case b {
        Full(ptr): mem_free(mov ptr)
        Empty: noop()
    }
}
proc main() i32 { return 0 }
